        "id": 1352056
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-28T00:01:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is true that those signals are common to ADL. However, since the logic and the hardware to manipulate those signals may vary, I opted to let the application handle it.\n\nFor this design `PWR_VCCST_PWRGD`, `PWR_PCH_PWROK` and `PWR_EC_PCH_SYS_PWROK` all depend on `PWR_ALL_SYS_PWRGD` state, but there may be another ADL design that would change this dependency or use external circuitry to generate signals.",
      "parentUuid": "0d3604b3_242a755e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 231,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 265,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "9dfdb51c3ab204a149c208383ca6fe897e79acdf",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "472b8e6a_2f8f95aa",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/nissa/src/board_power.c",
        "patchSetId": 29
      },
      "lineNbr": 265,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-28T00:12:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The PWROK generation flow diagram shows that VCCST_PWRGD, PCH_PWROK,and SYS_PWROK should always be gated on ALL_SYS_PWRGD.\n\nMaking this board specific seems unnecessary. It\u0027s better to add board specific hooks later, only if needed.\n\nThe non-PWRSEQ driver code is currently handling SYS_PWROK and VCCST_PWRGD in the shared ADL code.  `board_ap_power_assert_pch_power_ok()` handles the PCH_PWROK - but it this should probably be moved to the shared ADL code too.",
      "parentUuid": "5859e106_e18e3341",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 231,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 265,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "9dfdb51c3ab204a149c208383ca6fe897e79acdf",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
